\fIqmaint\fR performs package\-management housekeeping tasks and is a C
reimplementation of Portage's \fBemaint\fR. It operates on a named
\fImodule\fR with either the \fB\-\-check\fR or \fB\-\-fix\fR action.
.P
The available modules are:
.TP
.B binhost
Check that the local \fIPKGDIR/Packages\fR index agrees with the binary
packages on disk; \fB\-\-fix\fR regenerates the index (see also
\fBqmerge\fR(1) \fB\-\-index\fR).
.TP
.B moves
Apply the outstanding package and slot moves from the repositories'
update records to the installed package database.
.TP
.B news
Reconcile GLEP\ 42 news bookkeeping (see \fBqnews\fR(1)).
.TP
.B env
Regenerate the environment (\fI/etc/profile.env\fR and friends) from
\fI/etc/env.d\fR, equivalent to \fBenv\-update\fR(1).
.P
With neither \fB\-\-check\fR nor \fB\-\-fix\fR, \fB\-\-check\fR is
assumed. A check that finds nothing prints nothing and exits
successfully: the exit status, not the output, is the result signal.